# Contact form delivery - no third-party service.
# Copy to .env on the server and pass to Docker with:  docker run --env-file .env ...
#
# Every enquiry is first saved to DATA_DIR/contact-submissions.jsonl (mounted volume, see README),
# then emailed by this server itself. With nothing set below it connects directly to the MX host
# of CONTACT_TO on port 25 (DigitalOcean blocks this until you ask support to open it).

# CONTACT_TO=support@ztplsolutions.com
# CONTACT_FROM=ZTPL website <noreply@ztplsolutions.com>
# MAIL_HOSTNAME=mail.ztplsolutions.com     # EHLO name; should match the droplet's reverse DNS (PTR)

# Sign outgoing mail with your own DKIM key (publish the public key in DNS at <selector>._domainkey).
# Put the private key on one line with literal \n between lines.
# DKIM_SELECTOR=mail
# DKIM_PRIVATE_KEY=

# Optional: hand off to a mail server you run yourself (e.g. Postfix on the droplet) instead of direct-to-MX.
# MAIL_RELAY_HOST=host.docker.internal
# MAIL_RELAY_PORT=25
# MAIL_RELAY_USER=
# MAIL_RELAY_PASS=

# Where submissions are stored (the production image already sets /data).
# DATA_DIR=/data
